# A lens whose focus is a library's type: `put` writes a Fraction into the file and `get` gives it back inside an
# Entry. Building the Fraction in `get` is a call into the library, no occurrence: the Fraction it gives is a library's
# value, from beyond, and no name holds it. `put`'s Fraction is its parameter `amount`, another value.

route books.ledger.Ledger
step Ledger()/Ledger()
step Ledger()/Ledger.put
step Ledger()/Ledger.get
step Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry()

line entry > Ledger()/Ledger() call
line entry > Ledger()/Ledger.put call
line entry > Ledger()/Ledger.get call
line Ledger()/Ledger() > Ledger@Ledger()/Ledger() value
known #74 line Ledger > Ledger()/Ledger.put value   # the caller's instance: every method runs on it
known #74 line Ledger > Ledger()/Ledger.get value
known #127 line Fraction·amount > Ledger()/Ledger.put value      # #127
line Ledger()/Ledger.put > Disk(self.path) own
line Disk(self.path) > Ledger()/Ledger.get own
line Fraction > Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() value
line Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() > Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() value
line Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() > Ledger()/Ledger.get value
line Ledger()/Ledger.get > Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get value

home Ledger@Ledger()/Ledger() Ledger()
known #74 home Ledger Ledger()
known #127 home Fraction·amount Ledger()
home Fraction Ledger()
home Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get/Entry() Ledger()/Ledger.get
home Entry@Ledger()/Ledger.get Ledger()

side entry left
side Disk(self.path) between

# #127: put's parameter loses its name and becomes the Fraction get builds, one value taken by both
known #127 extra line Fraction > Ledger()/Ledger.put value

# what the constructor builds goes back to its caller: Atlas runs the methods on it instead of the caller's instance
known #74 extra line Ledger@Ledger()/Ledger() > Ledger()/Ledger.put value
known #74 extra line Ledger@Ledger()/Ledger() > Ledger()/Ledger.get value
